= Relationships is simple but hard
For some reason, this is the advice that I think a lot of people who find
happiness at a certain age learn, and I wanted to write about it on my blog.

I had an argument with my mom, as I always do, so I called a monk and he
suggested two things:
1. Intend to find small ways to be nice to her every day. Do small things like
   wash the dishes for her, or just complimenting her.
2. When she triggers me or is about to trigger me in an argument, I just walk
   away before I get to a boiling point. Arguing is just dumb at that point.


This is a common relationship strategy you'll find in a lot of places beyond
Buddhism. My manager and my grandmother suggested step 2 to me as well!
Somehow, all of these people, from different walks of life, with no
relationship(or some relationship to each other in teh case of my grandma and
the monk) to each other, converged on the same life advice, so there must be
something true to it! So I wanted to examine it on this blog on why these two
steps, are so simple, yet so hard to do for me specifically.
